// scratch after on_retire returns.
//
// The CSR sweep is safe on the drain side because a `csrr` of a CSR the hart
// implements never faults, and the caps table is exact -- the one over-claimed
// CSR (mcountermask_m 0x7D1, whose csrr raised cmderr on the M-only premium
// and aborted the whole batch) is UMODE-gated now. The RESTORE sweep stays
// off: a csrrw can still fault on read-only/WARL-illegal fields (see the
// simulator's resume NOTE).
void set_block_store_drain(bool on)
{
  drain_.set_gpr_block_store(on);
  drain_.set_fpr_block_store(on);
  drain_.set_csr_sweep(on);
}

